    "question": {
      ":question/id": "2cb0da35-813c-5399-9bc6-28691175dc37",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is a lower triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $A$ is a matrix for which all entries *above* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -5 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -10 & -6 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is a lower triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $B$, $C$, $D$, and $E$ each have at least one non-zero entry above the diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}-8 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -8 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 5 & -9 \\\\ -8 & -7 & 0 \\\\ 9 & -6 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -7 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not lower triangular matrices.",
