      ":question/id": "b681ac56-de9b-5a85-8f4a-e7c3185f5df7",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following is an upper triangular matrix?",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Notice that $E$ is a matrix for which all entries *below* the diagonal are $0$'s:\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 8 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 11 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nHence, it is an upper triangular matrix. \n\nBy contrast, matrices $A$, $B$, $C$, and $D$ each have at least one non-zero entry below the diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 6 & -11 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 10 \\\\ -2 & -3 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nC=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nD=\\begin{bmatrix}-9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSo, they are not upper triangular matrices.",
